---
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import DebugDock from "../../components/DebugDock.astro";

const siteTitle = "Baseline preferences – La Familia";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{siteTitle}</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        --text: #1f2933;
        --muted: #5b6570;
        --border: #d7dce1;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --accent: #2f5d7c;
        --background: #f6f7f9;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: "Inter", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        color: var(--text);
        background: var(--background);
      }

      main {
        max-width: 960px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 64px 24px 104px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 32px;
      }

      h1,
      h2 {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 2.4rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      p {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 18px;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .section {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 28px 32px;
      }

      .back-link {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .back-link:hover {
        color: var(--text);
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      .subtitle {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        max-width: 720px;
      }

      .note {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.98rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <DebugDock />
    <main>
      <PageHeader title="Baseline travel preferences" backHref="../../" backLabel="← Back to overview">
        <p>
          This travel archive exists to support thoughtful, long-term planning rather than
          inspiration or presentation. It reflects how we evaluate, structure and secure our trips
          — not just where we go.
        </p>
        <p>
          We travel as a family of five, with older children and young adults. This shapes
          everything: pace, safety, logistics and expectations. We value a calm, predictable
          framework that allows us to relax and be present once the journey has started.
        </p>
        <p>
          Control and preparation are not opposites to discovery for us — they are prerequisites.
          We prefer to secure the main structure of a trip in advance: flights, primary
          accommodation, key transfers and major segments. Clear holding points make the journey
          feel safe and manageable, especially when traveling long-haul as a family.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the same time, we actively seek authentic experiences, understood as places and
          settings that feel grounded in local life rather than designed for display. This often
          means:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>choosing traditional or locally rooted accommodation for part of a trip</li>
          <li>prioritising genuine food settings over polished dining concepts</li>
          <li>allowing different parts of a journey to serve different purposes</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Authenticity does not have to mean rustic, remote or uncomfortable. It means real, not staged.</p>
        <p>
          We are not opposed to well-known sights or landmarks. If something is culturally or
          historically significant, we are happy to include it. However, when two experiences offer
          similar value, we generally prefer the less touristic, less performative option — which
          often turns out to be both calmer and better.
        </p>
        <p>From a logistical perspective, we travel conservatively:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>We prefer established routes and reliable infrastructure</li>
          <li>We choose known, reputable airlines for long-haul travel</li>
          <li>Transfers should be safe, predictable and easy to understand</li>
          <li>
            On return journeys, we often include a final night close to the airport as a buffer if
            the last travel day is long or complex
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Accommodation matters. When possible, we prefer to stay together as a group rather than
          split across multiple rooms or locations. This supports both practical logistics and the
          social aspect of traveling as a family.
        </p>
        <p>We generally prefer:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>fewer bases over frequent moves</li>
          <li>depth over breadth</li>
          <li>environments where activities happen within the setting rather than on top of it</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We actively avoid:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>party-oriented destinations</li>
          <li>highly performative or social-media-driven travel cultures</li>
          <li>places where nature or culture feels exhausted, staged or overcrowded</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Weather perfection is not a goal. Functionality is.</p>
        <p>
          A destination should work for what we want to do at that time, with conditions that allow
          plans to be executed without constant adjustment.
        </p>
        <p>
          This baseline is intentionally non-specific. Seasonal priorities, thematic focus and
          concrete constraints are defined separately.
        </p>
      </PageHeader>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
